on, somatic hypermutation and class switching.", "front": "Processes occurring in germinal centres?"}, {"back": "A: CD4 or CD8 single positive (SP) T cells.", "front": "Form in which mature T cells exit the thymus?"}], "color": "blue", "folder": 0}, {"name": "Cells of the immune", "cards": [{"back": "A : Combat helminths, involved in allergic reactions, promote IgE production", "front": "Th2 cells?"}, {"back": "A : Thymic cortex", "front": "Where does positive selection of T cells occur?"}, {"back": "A : CD28 on the T cell and B7 on the APC", "front": "Molecules involved in co-stimulation?"}, {"back": "A : Thymic medulla; establishes central tolerance by eliminating strongly self-reactive T cells", "front": "Where does negative selection occur, and what does it establish?"}, {"back": "A : Fight intracellular pathogens by activating macrophages and inducing cell-mediated immunity", "front": "Th1 cells?"}, {"back": "A : Dendritic cells, macrophages and B cells", "front": "Professional APCs?"}, {"back": "A : CD40–CD40L signalling and cytokine secretion", "front": "Signalling between B cells and helper T cells in T-cell–dependent activation?"}, {"back": "A : Suppress immune responses to prevent autoimmunity and maintain tolerance", "front": "Treg cells?"}, {"back": "A : Chemotaxis → adherence and pseudopodium formation → engulfment and phagosome formation → phagosome–lysosome fusion → elimination or antigen processing", "front": "Steps of phagocytosis?"}, {"back": "A : Robust antibody responses, class switching, affinity maturation and memory B cells", "front": "Outcomes of T-cell–dependent activation?"}, {"back": "A : Fibroblasts and endothelial cells", "front": "Non-professional APCs?"}, {"back": "A : Apoptosis (death by neglect)", "front": "Fate of thymocytes that fail to recognise self-MHC?"}, {"back": "A : Becomes a CD4+ SP helper T cell (CD8 downregulated)", "front": "Fate of a DP thymocyte whose TCR recognises MHC-II?"}, {"back": "A : αβ TCR non-covalently associated with the CD3 signalling complex", "front": "Receptor complex on mature naïve CD4+ and CD8+ T cells?"}, {"back": "A : In germinal centres (spleen and LNs) during the primary immune response", "front": "Where are memory B cells generated?"}, {"back": "A : Toll-like receptor 9 (TLR9)", "front": "RBC surface receptor for nucleic acid sensing?"}, {"back": "A : Immune cell that captures, digests and displays foreign protein fragments on MHC molecules to activate T cells", "front": "Antigen-presenting cell (APC)?"}, {"back": "A : Perforin forms pores; granzymes enter the cytosol", "front": "Perforin vs granzymes?"}, {"back": "A : Medullary thymic epithelial cells and dendritic cells", "front": "Cells presenting self-peptides during negative selection?"}, {"back": "A : IgM (generally no immunological memory)", "front": "Antibody predominantly induced by T-cell–independent activation?"}, {"back": "A : T-cell dependent and T-cell independent", "front": "Two types of B-cell activation?"}, {"back": "A : Th1, Th2, Th17, Tfh and Treg", "front": "Principal CD4+ T helper subsets?"}, {"back": "A : Becomes a CD8+ SP cytotoxic T cell (CD4 downregulated)", "front": "Fate of a DP thymocyte whose TCR recognises MHC-I?"}, {"back": "A : DP thymocytes must recognise self-MHC with low to moderate affinity", "front": "Requirement for passing positive selection?"}, {"back": "A : Cross-presentation and enhanced APC activation, often dependent on CD4+ T-cell help", "front": "Antigens from non-replicating viruses require what to activate CD8+ T cells?"}, {"back": "A : Monocytes (macrophages, dendritic cells), neutrophils and eosinophils", "front": "Key phagocytic cells?"}, {"back": "A : They lack antigen-presenting capacity, cytokine synthesis and proliferative responses", "front": "Why are RBCs not classical immune cells?"}, {"back": "A : Complement interactions, immune complex transport, modulation of inflammatory mediators and nucleic acid sensing", "front": "How do RBCs influence immunit