y is colostrum important for a newborn?"}, {"back": "\\"In a living thing\\"", "front": "What does \\"in vivo\\" mean in the final slide?"}, {"back": "Macrophages, granulocytes, T cells, and B cells, which may aid local immune defence and immunoregulation, especially in the gastrointestinal tract", "front": "Which immune cells are found in human milk and may transfer to the breast-fed infant?"}, {"back": "\\"Out of a living thing\\"", "front": "What does \\"ex vivo\\" mean in the final slide?"}, {"back": "\\"In glass\\"", "front": "What does \\"in vitro\\" mean in the final slide?"}, {"back": "Red blood cells, plasma, and platelets", "front": "Which blood components are returned to the body during leukapheresis?"}, {"back": "Transfer of primed or sensitised immune cells, particularly lymphocytes, from an immune individual to a recipient to confer antigen-specific immune function", "front": "What is adoptive immunity?"}, {"back": "Donor compatibility, timing of transplantation, risk of graft-versus-host disease (GvHD), conditioning regimen, and the patient's clinical condition", "front": "Which factors influence successful HSCT outcomes?"}, {"back": "An immunotherapeutic strategy where immune effector cells are collected, expanded and/or genetically modified ex vivo, then reinfused into the patient to enhance immune responses", "front": "What is adoptive cell therapy (ACT)?"}], "color": "blue", "folder": 0}], "folders": [{"icon": "stethoscope", "name": "Micro", "color": "blue", "parent": null}]}	2026-11-27 09:12:09.144282+00	folder	e30b86c4-7515-46e7-bcda-f3b139361e87	\N	1ee99020-5a2f-4701-bdf1-ec41b9d24eac
