ff58372a	Micro	{"decks": [{"name": "intro", "cards": [{"back": "A: Yolk sac (weeks 3–5 of gestation).", "front": "First site of haematopoiesis in early embryogenesis?"}, {"back": "A: Afferent lymphatic vessels.", "front": "Vessels through which lymph enters a lymph node?"}, {"back": "A: Peyer’s patches and mesenteric lymph nodes.", "front": "Examples of gut-associated lymphoid tissue (GALT)?"}, {"back": "A: Lymph nodes, spleen and mucosa-associated lymphoid tissues (MALT).", "front": "Examples of secondary lymphoid organs?"}, {"back": "A: Spleen.", "front": "Principal secondary lymphoid organ for filtration of blood-borne antigens and pathogens?"}, {"back": "A: Cortex, paracortex and medulla (enclosed within a fibrous capsule).", "front": "Three structural regions of a lymph node?"}, {"back": "A: Sites where mature lymphocytes encounter antigens, become activated and initiate immune responses.", "front": "What are secondary (peripheral) lymphoid organs?"}, {"back": "A: Apoptosis.", "front": "Fate of DP cells that fail positive selection?"}, {"back": "A: B cells organised into primary follicles.", "front": "What does the lymph node cortex contain?"}, {"back": "A: Lymph = Local (tissue infections); Spleen = Systemic (blood infections).", "front": "Mnemonic: Lymph = ? / Spleen = ?"}, {"back": "A: RBCs and platelets.", "front": "Blood components normally absent from lymph?"}, {"back": "A: Weeks 20–24 of gestation (replacing foetal liver).", "front": "When does bone marrow become the dominant site of haematopoiesis?"}, {"back": "A: CD4– CD8– double negative (DN) T-lineage cells.", "front": "ETPs differentiate into?"}, {"back": "A: Notch signals.", "front": "Signals ETPs receive from thymic epithelial cells?"}, {"back": "A: Thymus medullary region.", "front": "Thymic region where DP cells undergo negative selection?"}, {"back": "A: Bone marrow and thymus.", "front": "Primary lymphoid organs in humans?"}, {"back": "A: Rich in T cells; contains high endothelial venules (HEV